# Caddy's global config and the snippets every site shares. Ticket 16.
# Per-service routing is `caddy` labels on each Service, which caddy-docker-proxy
# reads off the docker socket and merges into this file.
{
	acme_dns cloudflare {env.CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN}

	# No `email`: it would be either the human's address in a public repo, or a
	# parse error the moment secrets.env is missing. The cost is that Let's
	# Encrypt cannot send expiry warnings.
}

# Default-deny, ticket 05. `respond` sorts before `reverse_proxy` in Caddy's
# directive order, so this terminates the chain before the proxy sees anything.
(internal) {
	@external not remote_ip 192.168.1.0/24 100.64.0.0/10
	respond @external 403
}

# Declaring the wildcard is what makes Caddy issue one. Since 2.10 it prefers a
# managed wildcard over per-subdomain certificates, but only if the config names
# one -- otherwise this takes out a separate certificate per hostname. Caddy
# sorts wildcard-host blocks last, so a labelled hostname still wins.
*.rbrb.in {
	import internal
	respond "no service by that name" 404
}
